  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5121",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to NCI-H2081 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and also targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. Both pathways ultimately converge on NCI-H2081, indicating a potential dual role for Mollicellin N in modulating the biological response leading to this cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights a complex network of molecular interactions, where Mollicellin N may influence NCI-H2081 through distinct but related molecular mechanisms. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and NCI-H2081, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
